or 11  years Cavanaugh is proud he kicked the  habit  addiction is not an incurable disease he  says but a weakness to be conquered  around the world medication is used to  help people take their drug habit but we  do it without any tablets we're just  both quicker and easier  cold turkey  that's how Roman overcame his 13-year  addiction now he helps other addicts get  clean in the forests of Yekaterinburg  here they must be entirely  self-sufficient they have to survive  without any help  Roman takes us along to see for  ourselves  his job is to ensure that the recovering  addicts follow a strict daily routine  everyone has to do their bit it's like  living in a collective physical work is  good for people rehabilitation of  shouldn't be easy but it shouldn't be  too hard either  Arseniy has made it through the first  six months he misses city life and his  wife and three children but then he'd  rather spend one year without them than  the rest of his life when you get there  you just want to leave you want to get  away as quickly as possible by whatever  means then after a while when your body  starts to cleanse itself you realize  that you haven't lost everything in life  his drug abuse began at parties in st.  Petersburg it started with recreational  drugs than harder ones  I had problems at home my first wife  left me  Roman tells him to get a move on he  wants lunch served on time but then our  Sandi discovers a secret stash a new  arrival has hidden some eggs 18 eggs now  I know where all the eggs have got -  were you planning to sell them  embarrassed the boy brings them out he  wanted to use the money to buy something  to smoke Roman goes easy on him possibly  because we're filming lunch is ready  the ex-addicts have to prepare this  themselves Roman makes sure everything  is done properly  no one is given preferential treatment  that can lead to upsets  we all have different opinions but what  brings us together is our addiction you  talk about it a lot and that really  helps he hopes to be able to sell some  camera equipment in st. Petersburg in  about six months  Roman is optimistic about our Sandy's  future he's understood how essential it  is to make changes in his life there are  cameras in every room  Roman leaves nothing to chance right now  he lives a bit like an Orthodox priest  but at some point he wants to get back  to his old life again  he was once a shoemaker many in the West  say cold turkey is too hard for  recovering addicts but he says you can  only fight drugs by being tough Nicolae  however can't see any need to stop  taking drugs so far he's managed to keep  his addiction secret from his employer  he has enough drugs for the next few  days they've been a part of his life for  a long time  even when I just consider the last year  more and more young people are taking  drugs mainly because it's now so easy to  get a hold of them the chances of  getting caught are much lower here are  powerless to stop the spread of drugs  there are endless places to stash them  in Russia's major cities
 

